# Object Pooling

`Instantiate` and `Destroy` allocate, fragment the heap, and trigger GC — on WebGL the spikes are visible as hitches. Anything spawned repeatedly during gameplay must be pooled.

## When to pool

Pool any prefab spawned more than ~once per second during play: projectiles, hit VFX, floating damage text, audio one-shots, UI list items, cards, pickups.

Do **not** pool one-off objects (a boss, a screen, a loading panel) — a pool for a single instance is over-engineering.

## Pattern

Use `UnityEngine.Pool.ObjectPool<T>` (built-in, no package) or a simple stack-based pool. Deactivate on release, reset state on get.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — churn in a gameplay loop
private void Fire()
{
    var go = Instantiate(_projectilePrefab, muzzle.position, muzzle.rotation);
    Destroy(go, 3f);
}

// ✅ GOOD — pooled, pre-warmed
private ObjectPool<Projectile> _pool;

private void Awake()
{
    _pool = new ObjectPool<Projectile>(
        createFunc: () => Instantiate(_projectilePrefab, _poolRoot),
        actionOnGet: p => p.gameObject.SetActive(true),
        actionOnRelease: p => p.gameObject.SetActive(false),
        defaultCapacity: 32);
}

private void Fire()
{
    var p = _pool.Get();
    p.Launch(muzzle.position, muzzle.forward, ReturnToPool);
}

private void ReturnToPool(Projectile p)
{
    _pool.Release(p);
}
```

## Rules

- **Pre-warm at load.** Allocate the expected peak count during loading, not mid-combat. Size the pool from real gameplay numbers, not guesses.
- **Reset on get, not on release** when possible — the reset code then also covers freshly created instances.
- **Never `Destroy` a pooled object** from feature code; always release. A pooled object destroyed elsewhere corrupts the pool — release paths must be single-owner.
- **Trail renderers, particles, timers** must be cleared on release (`TrailRenderer.Clear()`, `ParticleSystem.Clear()`), or the next Get shows ghosts.
- Pools holding static references must be cleared in the project's static-reset hub (domain reload is disabled).

## Agent checklist

- [ ] Repeatedly spawned prefabs go through a pool, not Instantiate/Destroy
- [ ] Pool pre-warmed at load with realistic capacity
- [ ] State (trails, particles, velocities) reset so reused instances are clean
- [ ] Static pools registered in the static-reset hub
